# .supply-chain-guard.allow -- reviewed exceptions for testrelic-ai/supply-chain-guard.
#
# One entry per line, four TAB-separated fields:
#   <check-id> <TAB> <path> <TAB> <fingerprint> <TAB> <reason>
# The fingerprint is the fp= the guard prints for the finding. Every entry needs a
# concrete reason. An entry that no longer matches anything is itself a finding, so
# remove it when its package or script goes away. P1, P8, C1-C3 can never be
# allowlisted, and neither can anything under .github/workflows/.
#
# Reviewed 2026-10-01 for the guard adoption PR. For every S4 entry the lockfile's
# sha512 integrity was compared with the npm registry's dist.integrity for the exact
# locked version, and the install script was read from the registry tarball.
P7	packages/mcp/package.json	9c01062565976f63dd4af28cf8af92703954ba253b7856185e05b62ee4798de7	prepack=node scripts/mirror-skills.js regenerates the packaged agent-skill copy (packages/mcp/.agents/skills) from the tracked .agents/skills source so a clean CI checkout ships it (see CLAUDE.md, Agent Skill). prepack runs only when this repo packs or publishes (publish-npm.yml, gated on the guard); npm never runs it for consumers installing @testrelic/mcp from the registry. The script itself is scanned by P4/P5 like any build file.
S4	package-lock.json	696a1c4c44390d69fa9bf5787097d24230daae8bce74538f5117515410968210	better-sqlite3 11.10.0: optional dependency of @testrelic/mcp (L2 SQLite cache). install = 'prebuild-install || node-gyp rebuild --release' (downloads the prebuilt native addon or compiles it). Locked sha512 matches the npm registry.
S4	package-lock.json	58515e9681237126916ae9760b47d9f8c6dec27108af55b9e8ec8c145d4ab7dd	esbuild 0.28.1 (and 0.21.5 nested under vite): dev-only, pulled in by tsx and vite/vitest. postinstall = 'node install.js', which verifies the platform-specific @esbuild/* binary package (fetching it from registry.npmjs.org if the optional package is missing). Not in the published package or the Docker image. Locked sha512 of both versions matches the npm registry.
S4	package-lock.json	cc33522a44569c12018229c1a91624b820bb72c50f755f286a32e25a73fd1686	fsevents 2.3.3: dev-only, macOS-only optional dependency of rollup/vite/tsx (file watching). install = 'node-gyp rebuild'; os: darwin, so it is never installed on the Linux CI runners or in the Docker image. Locked sha512 matches the npm registry.
S4	package-lock.json	a0c5b82df3574557d47773172b3a927dfa0de14e12d5998aa2c106200291a685	hnswlib-node 3.0.0: optional dependency of @testrelic/mcp (L3 HNSW vector cache). install = 'node-gyp rebuild' compiles the native addon from the package's own sources. Locked sha512 matches the npm registry.
S4	package-lock.json	d42ec528920fc4c56c304ac1f2e9a608a38151d308adb1a6809fa01e50179ed8	protobufjs 7.6.4: transitive (@xenova/transformers -> onnxruntime-web -> onnx-proto), forced to 7.6.4 by the root package.json overrides (TEAI-281). postinstall = 'node scripts/postinstall', read from the registry tarball: it only prints a warning when a dependent uses the wrong version-range prefix. Locked sha512 matches the npm registry.
S4	package-lock.json	632e93023886160a2a5494cd49aeb72994fc61f6834355d175a423b99715a9df	sharp 0.32.6: via the optional @xenova/transformers (local embeddings). install downloads libvips 8.14.5 from github.com/lovell/sharp-libvips releases and checks it against the sha512 values pinned in sharp's own package.json (falls back to node-gyp). Locked sha512 matches the npm registry. Follow-up: sharp >= 0.33 ships libvips as @img/* npm packages, no download.
S4	package-lock.json	7d0dc28f8fd95654cf0704adc0bd3f33ee171a8fc48861f345c27cdf0aa8f65c	tree-sitter 0.22.4 (packages/mcp/node_modules): optional dependency of @testrelic/mcp (code map parsing). install = 'node-gyp-build' (uses the bundled prebuild, else compiles the vendored C sources). resolved + sha512 integrity added to the lockfile in this PR from the registry; the tarball hash was verified against dist.integrity.
S4	package-lock.json	88beabbefb63f882e0e5660e0d2961b99572c585f1cf1e47d0cb1ce70ce24726	tree-sitter-javascript 0.23.1: optional dependency of @testrelic/mcp (JS grammar for the code map). install = 'node-gyp-build' (bundled prebuild, else compile). Locked sha512 matches the npm registry.
S4	package-lock.json	f55f8e3d5676f1bf578ec16632085ba1f2fb5d51ff53490f1a756ca7124ff927	tree-sitter-typescript 0.23.2: optional dependency of @testrelic/mcp (TS grammar for the code map). install = 'node-gyp-build' (bundled prebuild, else compile). Locked sha512 matches the npm registry.
